---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Contribute | Awesome RNA Virus Tools">
  <main class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Community catalog</p>
    <h1>Contribute an entry</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Additions and corrections remain pull-request driven. Each entry is a small JSON
      file, so proposed changes stay reviewable and attributable.
    </p>

    <h2>Add or update an entry</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Fork the repository and create a focused branch.</li>
      <li>Add or edit one file in <code>entries/</code>, using a nearby entry of the same type as a guide.</li>
      <li>Run <code>npm run build</code>. Astro checks the entry schema as part of the build.</li>
      <li>Open a pull request describing the tool or literature record and its relevance to RNA virus research.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What belongs here</h2>
    <p>
      Publicly accessible software, databases, benchmarks, methods, and review literature
      with a clear role in RNA virus research are in scope. Descriptions should be factual,
      concise, and avoid promotional claims.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>